      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>A roaming creeper. It often appears on battlefields and other areas where a lot of blood is split. At one time, it was rooted in the earth like a normal plant. However, one day blood on the ground leaked into its roots, and the plant developed a thirst for it. Thus began its journey and transformation into a monster that attacks humans and animals for their blood. If you ever come across a fallen animal drained of its blood, a vamplant may not be too far away…</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 19, touch 11; flat-footed 18 (+1 Dex, +8 natural)</p><p>hp 60 [88] (8d8+24)</p><p>Fort +9, Ref +3, Will +4</p><p>Immune Plant traits; Resist earth 10, ice 10</p><p>Weakness Fire</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 20 ft.</p><p>Melee Slam +10 (1d8+6 plus grab and drain)</p><p>Special Attacks Constrict (1d8+6), Drain, Entangle, Leech</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 18, Dex 12, Con 16, Int -, Wis 14, Cha 9</p><p>Base Atk +6; CMB +10 (+14 grapple); CMD 21 (cannot be tripped)</p><p>Feats Improved Natural Attack (Slam)*</p><p>* Bonus Feat</p><p>SQ camouflage</p>"
      }
    },
